  "habitat": "Solitary or in pairs in dry, well-developed broad-leaved woodland and thornveld. It feeds in large trees, clambering on the outer branches.",
  "summary": "A fairly common woodland resident. Smaller than Green Wood-hoopoe, with a more decurved black bill and a shorter tail. The female and immature have brownish throats and breasts. During summer it calls pwep-pwep-pwep-pwep at half-second intervals. Newman does not describe the body colour. The Kemp paper name Scimitarbilled Woodhoopoe and the code RB were left unchanged.",
